<file path="supabase/seed/kestrel-vane-faq.md">
# Kestrel & Vane Ltd: Employee FAQ

Quick answers to common questions about the Kestrel & Vane Ltd Employee Handbook (version 3.2). If a question is not answered here, email the People team at people@kestrelandvane.example. Kestrel & Vane Ltd is a fictional company, and this FAQ is a synthetic sample document written for software testing.

## Leave

### Q1. How many days of annual leave do I get?

Full-time employees get 26 days of paid annual leave in each leave year, and the leave year runs from 1 April to 31 March. You receive 2 extra days after 3 completed years of service and 4 extra days in total after 6 completed years, so a full-time employee with 6 completed years gets 30 days. Public holidays are in addition to this.

### Q2. Can I carry over unused leave?

Yes. Up to 5 days of unused leave can be carried over into the next leave year. You must use the carried-over days by 30 June, otherwise they are lost.

### Q3. How do I request leave?

Request leave in the People Hub. A manager normally answers within 4 working days. A request covering 10 or more consecutive working days needs at least 6 weeks' notice.

## Sickness

### Q4. What should I do if I am too ill to work?

Tell your line manager by 09:30 on the first day of absence. You need a medical certificate once an absence lasts more than 3 consecutive working days, and you send it to the People team. You get 12 days at full pay each leave year.

## Working pattern

### Q5. How many days a week do I have to be in the office?

At least 2 days a week, and the company's anchor days are Tuesday and Thursday. During the probation period it is 4 days a week.

### Q6. Can I work from another country?

Yes, for up to 20 working days per calendar year, but you need written approval from the Head of People. Send your request at least 5 weeks before you travel.

### Q7. When do I get the home-office stipend?

New employees get a one-off stipend of $450. It is paid with the first payroll after your probation period ends, and the probation period lasts 6 months.

## Expenses and travel

### Q8. How much can I claim for a business trip to Berlin?

Berlin is a Tier 2 city, so you can claim $60 per day for meals and up to $190 per night for a hotel.

### Q9. How soon must I submit an expense claim?

Submit it in the Tallybook portal within 30 days of the expense. The Finance Office rejects older claims unless it agreed an exception in advance.

## IT security

### Q10. What do I do if I lose my laptop?

Report it to the Security Desk within 1 hour of noticing the loss. Email security@kestrelandvane.example or call extension 4417.

## Speaking up, pay and benefits

### Q11. How do I raise a concern about misconduct?

Use the Speak Up line, which is run by an independent provider, or email speakup@kestrelandvane.example. Every report is acknowledged within 2 working days, and investigations are normally completed within 20 working days of the investigator being assigned.

### Q12. When am I paid, and what benefits do I get?

Salaries are paid on the 25th of each month, or on the Friday before when the 25th falls on a weekend. The company contributes 6% of base salary to your pension if you contribute at least 4%, and 7% in total if you contribute 8% or more. Each employee also has a learning budget of $1,200 per leave year.
</file>

<file path="tests/unit/chunking-normalize.test.ts">
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";
import { PIPELINE_VERSION, normalizePageText } from "@/lib/chunking/normalize";

const FAMILY = "👨‍👩‍👧‍👦"; // man ZWJ woman ZWJ girl ZWJ boy

describe("PIPELINE_VERSION", () => {
  it("is 1 (documents.pipeline_version default)", () => {
    expect(PIPELINE_VERSION).toBe(1);
  });
});

describe("normalizePageText whitespace rules", () => {
  it("converts CRLF and lone CR to LF", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a\r\nb\rc\nd")).toBe("a\nb\nc\nd");
  });

  it("converts tabs and NBSP to ordinary spaces", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a\tb\u00a0c")).toBe("a b c");
  });

  it("collapses runs of spaces", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a     b \t \u00a0 c")).toBe("a b c");
  });

  it("strips trailing spaces from each line", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("one   \ntwo \t\nthree")).toBe("one\ntwo\nthree");
  });

  it("collapses 3 or more newlines to exactly 2 and keeps 1 and 2", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a\n\n\n\nb\n\nc\nd")).toBe("a\n\nb\n\nc\nd");
  });

  it("treats whitespace-only lines as empty when collapsing newlines", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a\n  \n \t \nb")).toBe("a\n\nb");
  });

  it("trims the page", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("  \n\n  hello  \n\n ")).toBe("hello");
  });

  it("returns an empty string for empty and whitespace-only input", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("")).toBe("");
    expect(normalizePageText(" \n\t\u00a0\r\n ")).toBe("");
  });

  it("maps form feed and Unicode line separators to newlines", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a\fb\u2028c\u2029d\u0085e")).toBe(
      "a\nb\nc\nd\ne",
    );
  });
});

describe("normalizePageText Unicode rules", () => {
  it("applies NFKC: ligatures and compatibility forms", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("o\ufb03ce \ufb01le")).toBe("office file");
  });

  it("composes combining characters (NFKC)", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("cafe\u0301")).toBe("caf\u00e9");
  });

  it("removes soft hyphens", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("co\u00adop\u00aderate")).toBe("cooperate");
  });

  it("removes zero width space, word joiner, BOM and bidi marks", () => {
    expect(
      normalizePageText("\ufeffa\u200bb\u2060c\u200ed\u200fe\u202af\u2066g"),
    ).toBe("abcdefg");
  });

  it("removes control characters, including NUL (not storable in Postgres)", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a\u0000b\u0007c\u007fd\u0090e")).toBe("abcde");
  });

  it("preserves U+200D (ZWJ) and U+200C (ZWNJ)", () => {
    const text = "a\u200db\u200cc";
    expect(normalizePageText(text)).toBe(text);
  });

  it("preserves the Persian half-space (ZWNJ) in real words", () => {
    const word = "می\u200cخواهم";
    expect(normalizePageText(`${word} ${word}`)).toBe(`${word} ${word}`);
  });

  it("preserves family emoji sequences intact", () => {
    const text = `Family ${FAMILY} here`;
    const out = normalizePageText(text);
    expect(out).toBe(text);
    expect(out).toContain("\u200d");
    expect([...FAMILY].filter((c) => c === "\u200d")).toHaveLength(3);
  });

  it("preserves variation selectors (emoji presentation)", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("\u2764\ufe0f")).toBe("\u2764\ufe0f");
  });

  it("replaces unpaired surrogates with U+FFFD and keeps valid pairs", () => {
    expect(normalizePageText("a\ud800b\udc00c😀d")).toBe("a\ufffdb\ufffdc😀d");
  });

  it("keeps CJK text; NFKC maps fullwidth ASCII punctuation but not 。", () => {
    // U+FF0C (fullwidth comma) and U+FF01 (fullwidth !) become ASCII under
    // NFKC; U+3002 (ideographic full stop) is left alone.
    expect(normalizePageText("你好，世界。\r\n再见！")).toBe(
      "你好,世界。\n再见!",
    );
  });
});

describe("normalizePageText idempotence", () => {
  const samples = [
    "",
    "plain text",
    "  \r\n\r\n\r\n a \u00a0\t b  \n\n\n\n c \r",
    "co\u00ad\u0301nfig e\u00ad\u0301 e\u0301\u00ad\u0301",
    "\u200b\u0301a \u200b \u0301",
    `x ${FAMILY}\u200d y \u200c z`,
    "o\ufb03ce \ufb01le \u2460 \u00bd \u2122 \u2026 \u3000x\u3000",
    "\ud800\udc00 \ud800 \udc00 a\ud83d",
    "\u1100\u1161\u11a8 \uac00\u11a8",
    "line \u2028 sep \u2029 para \u0085 nel \u000b vt \f ff",
    "\ufdfa \u3392 \ufb2c",
  ];

  it("returns the same string when applied twice (curated samples)", () => {
    for (const sample of samples) {
      const once = normalizePageText(sample);
      expect(normalizePageText(once)).toBe(once);
    }
  });

  it("returns the same string when applied twice (seeded random mixes)", () => {
    const alphabet = [
      "a",
      "e",
      "q",
      " ",
      " ",
      "\n",
      "\n",
      "\r",
      "\t",
      "\u00a0",
      "\u00ad",
      "\u200b",
      "\u200c",
      "\u200d",
      "\u0301",
      "\u0323",
      "\ufb01",
      "\u2028",
      "\ud83d",
      "\ude00",
      "😀",
      "你",
      "。",
      "\u1100",
      "\u1161",
      "\u11a8",
      "\ufe0f",
      "\ufeff",
      "\u0000",
    ];
    let seed = 12345;
    const next = (): number => {
      seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0;
      return seed / 2 ** 32;
    };
    for (let i = 0; i < 4000; i++) {
      const length = 1 + Math.floor(next() * 14);
      let s = "";
      for (let j = 0; j < length; j++) {
        s += alphabet[Math.floor(next() * alphabet.length)];
      }
      const once = normalizePageText(s);
      expect(normalizePageText(once), JSON.stringify(s)).toBe(once);
    }
  });
});
</file>

<file path="tests/unit/chunking-paginate.test.ts">
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";
import { chunkPages } from "@/lib/chunking/chunk-pages";
import { normalizePageText } from "@/lib/chunking/normalize";
import {
  DEFAULT_VIRTUAL_PAGE_CHARS,
  paginateText,
} from "@/lib/chunking/paginate-text";

function stripWhitespace(text: string): string {
  return text.replace(/\s+/g, "");
}

/** Text of exactly `length` characters made of words, no sentence punctuation. */
function paragraph(length: number, label: string): string {
  const base = "lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipiscing elit sed do ";
  let text = `${label} `;
  while (text.length < length + 5) text += base;
  text = text.slice(0, length);
  return text.endsWith(" ") ? `${text.slice(0, -1)}x` : text;
}

describe("paginateText", () => {
  it("defaults to 4000-character virtual pages", () => {
    expect(DEFAULT_VIRTUAL_PAGE_CHARS).toBe(4000);
  });

  it("returns [] for empty and whitespace-only text", () => {
    expect(paginateText("")).toEqual([]);
    expect(paginateText(" \n\t\r\n\u00a0 ")).toEqual([]);
  });

  it("puts short text on page 1, normalized", () => {
    expect(paginateText("Hello\r\nworld\u00a0!")).toEqual([
      { page: 1, text: "Hello\nworld !" },
    ]);
  });

  it("cuts a .txt file at paragraph boundaries near the target size", () => {
    const paragraphs = Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) =>
      paragraph(900, `P${i}`),
    );
    const pages = paginateText(paragraphs.join("\n\n"));
    // 4 paragraphs (3,602 chars) fit in a 4,000-char page; a 5th does not.
    expect(pages.map((p) => p.page)).toEqual([1, 2, 3]);
    expect(pages.map((p) => p.text)).toEqual([
      paragraphs.slice(0, 4).join("\n\n"),
      paragraphs.slice(4, 8).join("\n\n"),
      paragraphs.slice(8, 12).join("\n\n"),
    ]);
    expect(
      pages.every((p) => p.text.length <= DEFAULT_VIRTUAL_PAGE_CHARS),
    ).toBe(true);
  });

  it("keeps Markdown as plain text without parsing it", () => {
    const markdown = [
      "# Heading",
      "",
      "* item **bold** and `code`",
      "* [link](https://example.com)",
      "",
      "```",
      "const x = 1;",
      "```",
    ].join("\n");
    const pages = paginateText(markdown);
    expect(pages).toHaveLength(1);
    expect(pages[0].text).toBe(markdown);
  });

  it("normalizes before cutting (CRLF, NBSP, ligatures, soft hyphens)", () => {
    const raw = "ﬁrst\u00a0line\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nco\u00adop second line";
    expect(paginateText(raw)).toEqual([
      { page: 1, text: "first line\n\ncoop second line" },
    ]);
  });

  it("hard-cuts only when a paragraph is larger than the page size", () => {
    const token = "x".repeat(10000);
    const pages = paginateText(token);
    expect(pages.map((p) => p.text.length)).toEqual([4000, 4000, 2000]);
    expect(pages.map((p) => p.text).join("")).toBe(token);
  });

  it("prefers a sentence boundary over a hard cut inside an oversized paragraph", () => {
    const text = Array.from(
      { length: 400 },
      (_, i) => `Sentence ${String(i).padStart(3, "0")} is here.`,
    ).join(" ");
    const pages = paginateText(text, { virtualPageChars: 1000 });
    expect(pages.length).toBeGreaterThan(5);
    for (const page of pages.slice(0, -1)) {
      expect(page.text.endsWith("here.")).toBe(true);
    }
  });

  it("preserves all text across virtual page boundaries, with no loss or duplication", () => {
    const text = [
      Array.from({ length: 30 }, (_, i) =>
        paragraph(150 + i * 7, `A${i}`),
      ).join("\n\n"),
      "x".repeat(450),
      "这是一个测试句子。".repeat(80),
      "😀 end of the file 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦",
    ].join("\n\n");
    for (const virtualPageChars of [4000, 500, 97, 10, 4]) {
      const pages = paginateText(text, { virtualPageChars });
      expect(pages.every((p) => p.text.length <= virtualPageChars)).toBe(true);
      expect(pages.map((p) => p.page)).toEqual(pages.map((_, i) => i + 1));
      // Pages joined in order are the normalized text; only the blank-line
      // separators between pages are dropped.
      expect(stripWhitespace(pages.map((p) => p.text).join(""))).toBe(
        stripWhitespace(normalizePageText(text)),
      );
    }
  });

  it("never splits a surrogate pair at a hard cut", () => {
    const pages = paginateText("😀".repeat(1000), { virtualPageChars: 7 });
    for (const page of pages) {
      expect([...page.text].every((c) => c === "😀")).toBe(true);
    }
    expect(pages.map((p) => p.text).join("")).toBe("😀".repeat(1000));
  });

  it("produces pages that are already normalized", () => {
    const text = "Cafe\u0301 ﬁle\r\n\r\n\r\n".repeat(200);
    for (const page of paginateText(text, { virtualPageChars: 300 })) {
      expect(normalizePageText(page.text)).toBe(page.text);
    }
  });

  it("feeds chunkPages: chunk offsets index into the virtual page text", () => {
    const text = Array.from({ length: 60 }, (_, i) =>
      paragraph(500, `P${i}`),
    ).join("\n\n");
    const pages = paginateText(text);
    expect(pages.length).toBeGreaterThan(5);
    const chunks = chunkPages(pages);
    expect(chunks.length).toBeGreaterThan(pages.length);
    for (const chunk of chunks) {
      const page = pages[chunk.pageNumber - 1];
      expect(chunk.content).toBe(
        page.text.slice(chunk.charStart, chunk.charEnd),
      );
    }
    expect([...new Set(chunks.map((c) => c.pageNumber))]).toEqual(
      pages.map((p) => p.page),
    );
  });

  it("is deterministic", () => {
    const text = Array.from({ length: 50 }, (_, i) =>
      paragraph(333, `D${i}`),
    ).join("\n\n");
    expect(paginateText(text)).toEqual(paginateText(text));
  });

  it("throws on an invalid virtualPageChars", () => {
    for (const virtualPageChars of [0, 3, -5, 100.5, Number.NaN]) {
      expect(() => paginateText("text", { virtualPageChars })).toThrow(
        RangeError,
      );
